WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:06.260
- YouTube, Facebook, happy Sunday morning.

00:00:06.260 --> 00:00:08.270
Happy Father's Day to
all the dads out there.

00:00:08.270 --> 00:00:10.670
Jordan, you're right
there, good to see you.

00:00:10.670 --> 00:00:12.943
We can leave now Jordan
but you can walk with me.

00:00:12.943 --> 00:00:14.650
I just want to do a raw to the face

00:00:14.650 --> 00:00:16.490
video on this Sunday morning.

00:00:16.490 --> 00:00:17.690
We've been doing a lot of Keynotes,

00:00:17.690 --> 00:00:19.960
a lot of DailyVees for
YouTube and Facebook

00:00:19.960 --> 00:00:21.840
but just wanted to do a little rant

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:25.980
from the kind of, the
hip, right from the dome.

00:00:25.980 --> 00:00:29.130
Just want to thank you so much,
your comments are my oxygen.

00:00:29.130 --> 00:00:31.150
I say it over and over,
you'd be blown away

00:00:31.150 --> 00:00:34.980
by how much I breathe with feedback.

00:00:34.980 --> 00:00:37.040
To me getting that feedback from you guys

00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:40.020
is just amazing and I'm just
so grateful and thankful

00:00:40.020 --> 00:00:42.620
and just wanted to make
a raw kind of quick video

00:00:42.620 --> 00:00:44.950
just thanking you so, so,
so much for all of that.

00:00:44.950 --> 00:00:48.340
The community is the game,
the process is the game,

00:00:48.340 --> 00:00:50.920
and I've hit that kind
of quiet crescendo moment

00:00:50.920 --> 00:00:54.940
where I'm so in tune
with putting out content,

00:00:54.940 --> 00:00:57.310
putting it out there,
letting you guys consume it,

00:00:57.310 --> 00:00:59.730
reading your feedback in this viral loop

00:00:59.730 --> 00:01:01.480
and it just feels like I'm in that zone

00:01:01.480 --> 00:01:05.090
And every day I wish
for you guys out there

00:01:05.090 --> 00:01:07.070
in the world to find that same zone.

00:01:07.070 --> 00:01:09.360
And so, look for that
thing, find that thing,

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:12.580
and for me this community is that thing

00:01:12.580 --> 00:01:14.710
and I want to thank you
from the bottom of my heart.

00:01:14.710 --> 00:01:16.900
Thank you so much, have the
best, best rest of the weekend,

00:01:16.900 --> 00:01:19.920
have the best summer, flip, start things,

00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:22.980
produce content, but most of all listen.

00:01:22.980 --> 00:01:25.460
The audacity that everybody
wants likes, and comments,

00:01:25.460 --> 00:01:28.310
and subscribers but
doesn't want to then do

00:01:28.310 --> 00:01:30.070
for them what they want in return.

00:01:30.070 --> 00:01:33.830
The selfishness of give me
vanity, metrics, and social,

00:01:33.830 --> 00:01:37.350
and content, and digital, yet the key is

00:01:37.350 --> 00:01:39.710
if you listened and cared
about those individuals

00:01:39.710 --> 00:01:41.590
as much as what you wanted from them

00:01:41.590 --> 00:01:44.440
in likes and subscribers,
everything would be different.

00:01:44.440 --> 00:01:46.400
Please do not take things for granted

00:01:46.400 --> 00:01:48.550
and most of all do not take
your community for granted

00:01:48.550 --> 00:01:50.480
'cause it is the foundation
of your opportunity

00:01:50.480 --> 00:01:52.683
in this digital world, see ya.

